# .env.example — KEY NAMES ONLY. NEVER A VALUE.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is git-ignored and is never committed, never logged,
# never echoed, and never printed in a report or a transcript (PROCESS.md §8).
#
# ⚠️ NO SESSION MAY READ, PRINT, ECHO OR COMMIT A KEY VALUE. To confirm a key exists,
# read only its NAME. `make check-roles` fails if any line in THIS file carries a value,
# and scans every tracked file for secret-shaped strings.
#
# ⚠️ NO PAYMENT METHOD IS ATTACHED TO EITHER PROVIDER ACCOUNT, and that is the project's
# hard cost guarantee rather than an inconvenience: exceeding a limit returns HTTP 429 and
# the runner stops — IT CANNOT BILL. (CONTEXT.md §13.1, PROCESS.md §8.) The ₹2,500 reserve
# is RESERVE ONLY; the run is designed to cost ₹0. If the reserve is ever touched, the
# amount and the reason go in INCIDENTS.md.
#
# ⚠️ A 429 MEANS THE WINDOW IS ALREADY SPENT: a session STOPS and reports. It never
# retries into another lane. (The runner backs off and re-queues WITHIN its own lane.)

# ── Groq — the three ladder lanes (L1 gpt-oss-20b, L2 qwen3.8-27b, L3 gpt-oss-120b) ──
# Reserved for the ladder windows from 31 August. No build session may spend on them.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# ── Google — the reference attacker, the gate judge, the user simulator, the solver ──
# Gemma 4 26B/31B are reserved for the sweep from 31 August.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ── Notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# * There is no `rzp_live_` or `rzp_test_` key anywhere in this project. The world is a
#   MOCK. Every input is synthetic mock-world payment data with no real credentials and
#   no real customer data — which is what makes the free tiers' data terms acceptable,
#   and the README says so rather than burying it.
# * The CaMeL comparator (CONTEXT.md §8.5) has no `base_url` override, so it reaches
#   Google through GOOGLE_API_KEY or it does not run — which is exactly what RUN-1's
#   90-minute timeboxed branch test decides. Branch B is published as a RESULT.
